final_image_tex = SubResource("Resource_bdje5")
province = 49
blurb = "Depicts travelers looking out at Mount Fudesute on the Tōkaidō near the Saka no Shita post station (present-day Kameyama, Mie prefecture).

The name \"fudesute\" literally means \"to throw away the brush\". According to folklore, during the Muromachi period, when the famed painter Kanō Motonobu attempted to paint this mountain with its landscape of strongly-shaped rocks and groves of maple, pine, and azaleas, the shifting light caused by clouds and haze caused him to throw down his paintbrush in frustration.

Today, there are only a few private residences left at the site of the former post station, and very little historical architecture. The only thing that marks the former site is a stone marker built by the former town of Seki, now part of the city of Kameyama."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://6kpsqyb2pk7a"
